(954594, 109615, 10390, '<td valign="top">Outstanding shot, everything works well together here, the color in the blurred backround, the backlight and the use of fill-in flash (?).  Maybe a centered version would have been even better as its body faces a bit out of the frame to the right and its face out of the frame to the left. Congrats on the ribbon, great collection you have.</td>', 'Outstanding shot, everything works well together here, the color in the blurred backround, the backlight and the use of fill-in flash (?).  Maybe a centered version would have been even better as its body faces a bit out of the frame to the right and its face out of the frame to the left. Congrats on the ribbon, great collection you have.', '2004-10-11 15:59:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(954647, 109615, 4388, '<td valign="top">Great shot Danny! A lot of your photos have that warm look to them with exceptional lighting. What lens and did you use a fill flash? R</td>', 'Great shot Danny! A lot of your photos have that warm look to them with exceptional lighting. What lens and did you use a fill flash? R', '2004-10-11 16:47:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(954654, 109615, 4493, '<td valign="top">Thanks Richard,<br/> <br/>I used my 70-200 f/2.8 VR with a 2x teleconverter. Mother nature provided the backlight, I used my sb800 speedlight at probably -0.3 for fill flash. I actually wasn''t thrilled with this shot when I took it, but with my 2 hour visit to the zoo that morning, it was the best I had. I do tend to warm my shots either in camera with my white balance setting, or in Nikon Capture Editor or PS CS. I got use to the warmth of my fuji 602, and have continued the feel with my Nikons.<br/> <br/>-danny<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by goodtempo:</b></div><hr/><i> Great shot Danny! A lot of your photos have that warm look to them with exceptional lighting. What lens and did you use a fill flash? R </i></td></tr></table><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-10-11 15:55:55.</i></td>', 'Thanks Richard, I used my 70-200 f/2.8 VR with a 2x teleconverter. Mother nature provided the backlight, I used my sb800 speedlight at probably -0.3 for fill flash. I actually wasn''t thrilled with this shot when I took it, but with my 2 hour visit to the zoo that morning, it was the best I had. I do tend to warm my shots either in camera with my white balance setting, or in Nikon Capture Editor or PS CS. I got use to the warmth of my fuji 602, and have continued the feel with my Nikons. -danny Originally posted by goodtempo: Great shot Danny! A lot of your photos have that warm look to them with exceptional lighting. What lens and did you use a fill flash? R ', '2004-10-11 16:55:20.000000', '2004-10-11 16:55:55.000000', 0),
(954748, 108898, 714, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Imagineer:</b></div><hr/><i> "Taken out of town about 20 miles"? That''s a great zoom you''ve got!  : )<br/> <br/>Great image, well spotted. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>LOL</td>', 'Originally posted by Imagineer: "Taken out of town about 20 miles"? That''s a great zoom you''ve got!  : ) Great image, well spotted.   LOL', '2004-10-11 17:48:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(954751, 108898, 714, '<td valign="top">Thanks folks for all the wonderful comments.  I wish I got a better shot so I could get a print.</td>', 'Thanks folks for all the wonderful comments.  I wish I got a better shot so I could get a print.', '2004-10-11 17:49:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(954796, 109140, 21245, '<td valign="top">Thank you to everyone who took the time to vote and especially comment.  Submissions I have seen from past challanges have been very creative, and I''ve seen some photographers who shoot a particular style and find ways to alter it only enough to be applicable to a given challenge.  I like shooting people, and kids are the wildest people I know.  I understand the low marks, but had fun taking the picture and always enjoy participating in challenges.  Thanks again for the feedback!</td>', 'Thank you to everyone who took the time to vote and especially comment.  Submissions I have seen from past challanges have been very creative, and I''ve seen some photographers who shoot a particular style and find ways to alter it only enough to be applicable to a given challenge.  I like shooting people, and kids are the wildest people I know.  I understand the low marks, but had fun taking the picture and always enjoy participating in challenges.  Thanks again for the feedback!', '2004-10-11 18:37:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(954884, 109604, 2310, '<td valign="top">Thanks everyone!  I spent about 3 hours in the rain, crawling through mud to get ths shot of this silly toad...<br/> <br/>Nice catch <b>Gatorguy</b>...It was chilly and he was pretty much a perfect model...letting me put him wherever and staying for a while.  I hope I didn''t stress him too much...he calmly hopped back under his log when I put him back so I think he was ok with the whole ordeal... :~)<br/> <br/></td>', 'Thanks everyone!  I spent about 3 hours in the rain, crawling through mud to get ths shot of this silly toad... Nice catch Gatorguy...It was chilly and he was pretty much a perfect model...letting me put him wherever and staying for a while.  I hope I didn''t stress him too much...he calmly hopped back under his log when I put him back so I think he was ok with the whole ordeal... :~) ', '2004-10-11 19:47:27.000000', NULL, 0),
